1
0:00:00,300 --> 0:00:03,030
Private Tickets for the Midnight Buildathon,

2
0:00:03,030 --> 0:00:03,470
Wave 3.

3
0:00:03,470 --> 0:00:05,640
Normal ticketing leaks who you are,

4
0:00:05,640 --> 0:00:06,880
which seat is yours,

5
0:00:06,880 --> 0:00:08,560
and every event you attend.

6
0:00:08,560 --> 0:00:08,870
Here,

7
0:00:08,870 --> 0:00:10,980
you prove you hold a valid ticket,

8
0:00:10,980 --> 0:00:12,040
and nothing else.

9
0:00:12,840 --> 0:00:16,980
Under the hood it's one Compact contract with three circuits:

10
0:00:16,980 --> 0:00:17,870
issue ticket,

11
0:00:17,870 --> 0:00:18,480
check in,

12
0:00:18,480 --> 0:00:19,700
and resell ticket.

13
0:00:20,500 --> 0:00:20,890
First,

14
0:00:20,890 --> 0:00:22,460
the host issues tickets.

15
0:00:22,460 --> 0:00:25,910
Each guest keeps a secret and hands over only a hash,

16
0:00:25,910 --> 0:00:27,610
so the host never sees it.

17
0:00:27,610 --> 0:00:29,690
Alice and Bob each get a ticket.

18
0:00:30,490 --> 0:00:31,250
At the door,

19
0:00:31,250 --> 0:00:32,200
Alice scans in.

20
0:00:32,200 --> 0:00:36,130
A zero-knowledge Merkle proof shows her ticket is in the tree,

21
0:00:36,130 --> 0:00:39,110
and the chain learns only a one-time nullifier.

22
0:00:39,910 --> 0:00:41,620
Scan the same ticket again,

23
0:00:41,620 --> 0:00:43,260
and the nullifier repeats,

24
0:00:43,260 --> 0:00:44,970
so the contract rejects it.

25
0:00:45,770 --> 0:00:49,140
A stranger with no ticket can't build a valid proof,

26
0:00:49,140 --> 0:00:50,880
so Mallory is rejected too.

27
0:00:51,680 --> 0:00:52,720
Resale is capped.

28
0:00:52,720 --> 0:00:55,690
Bob tries to sell for one hundred twenty dollars,

29
0:00:55,690 --> 0:00:57,270
over the fifty dollar cap,

30
0:00:57,270 --> 0:00:58,060
and it fails.

31
0:00:58,060 --> 0:01:00,370
At forty five dollars it goes through.

32
0:01:00,370 --> 0:01:01,590
The old ticket dies,

33
0:01:01,590 --> 0:01:04,020
and a fresh one is minted for the buyer.

34
0:01:04,820 --> 0:01:05,480
Meanwhile,

35
0:01:05,480 --> 0:01:08,870
the public ledger holds only hashes and nullifiers.

36
0:01:08,870 --> 0:01:10,130
There are no names,

37
0:01:10,130 --> 0:01:10,990
no addresses,

38
0:01:10,990 --> 0:01:12,450
and no ticket numbers.

39
0:01:13,250 --> 0:01:14,800
All twelve tests pass,

40
0:01:14,800 --> 0:01:16,920
covering every rejection path:

41
0:01:16,920 --> 0:01:18,050
the double scan,

42
0:01:18,050 --> 0:01:18,760
no ticket,

43
0:01:18,760 --> 0:01:20,310
a forged resale count,

44
0:01:20,310 --> 0:01:21,580
an over-cap price,

45
0:01:21,580 --> 0:01:23,410
and resale after check-in.

46
0:01:23,410 --> 0:01:25,530
The real Midnight proof server

47
0:01:25,530 --> 0:01:27,790
then generates all three proofs,

48
0:01:27,790 --> 0:01:29,620
about five kilobytes each,

49
0:01:29,620 --> 0:01:30,820
in a few seconds.

50
0:01:31,620 --> 0:01:33,400
Built solo by Mark Flores,

51
0:01:33,400 --> 0:01:34,150
in Compact.

52
0:01:34,150 --> 0:01:35,650
It runs locally today,

53
0:01:35,650 --> 0:01:37,500
with a Preview deploy next.

54
0:01:37,500 --> 0:01:38,600
Private Tickets:

55
0:01:38,600 --> 0:01:39,760
prove you belong,

56
0:01:39,760 --> 0:01:41,600
without saying who you are.

